    [Doc][Misc] Add clean rebuild guidance after CANN version changes (#18215)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    After upgrading or downgrading CANN, previously compiled artifacts and
    cached build results may be incompatible with the updated environment.
    Reinstalling vLLM Ascend without cleaning them may reuse stale artifacts
    and lead to build or runtime compatibility issues.
    
    This PR adds a collapsible tip to the source installation guide
    explaining how to perform a clean rebuild when compatibility issues
    occur after a CANN version change. The guidance covers:
    
    - Removing previous build artifacts and caches (`csrc/build`,
    `csrc/build_out`, `csrc/build_cache`, and `build`).
    - Rebuilding custom kernels and reinstalling vLLM Ascend from source.
    - Handling custom build cache locations configured through
    `VLLM_ASCEND_BUILD_CACHE_DIR`.
    - Checking compatibility between CANN, `torch_npu`, and vLLM Ascend
    before rebuilding.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a documentation-only update; it does not change runtime
    behavior, APIs, or build logic.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Reviewed the documentation diff, including the placement of the
    collapsible tip under the source installation tab and its Markdown
    indentation. No functional or runtime tests were run because this change
    only updates documentation.
    
